---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getApp, COMPANY } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('shopkeep')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 22, 2026';
const sections = [
  { href: '#availability', label: 'Availability and readiness' },
  { href: '#identity', label: 'Sign-in and identity' },
  { href: '#media', label: 'Private media' },
  { href: '#offline', label: 'Offline limits' },
  { href: '#export', label: 'Exports and backups' },
  { href: '#deletion', label: 'Deletion and recreation' },
  { href: '#troubleshooting', label: 'Troubleshooting' },
  { href: '#contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  app={app}
  title={`${app.name} Support — ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with ShopKeep Apple and Microsoft sign-in, private photos and documents, offline limits, CSV/PDF/database exports, backups, account deletion, and current native readiness."
  path="/shopkeep/support"
  page="support"
  heading="ShopKeep Support"
  documentMeta={`Updated ${updatedDate} · Private web and native pre-release`}
  summary="ShopKeep has a private account-backed web app and a private native build for iPhone and iPad. Account deletion is implemented, but physical-device and App Store readiness checks remain open. There is no public App Store listing, TestFlight acquisition link, or announced price."
  sections={sections}
  evidenceNote="Support guidance was reviewed against the current live server, matching default-branch code, native lifecycle implementation, and release-readiness notes on August 22, 2026."
>
  <section id="availability" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Current availability and readiness</h2>
    <p class="legal-callout">
      ShopKeep’s server and deletion lifecycle are implemented and tested. The
      private native app is not yet App Store-ready: physical-device Apple and
      Microsoft sign-in and deletion checks, privacy-report reconciliation, and
      submission remain pending.
    </p>
    <p>
      Current private access does not imply a public beta, public App Store
      listing, price, or release date.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="identity" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Apple and Microsoft sign-in</h2>
    <p>
      Apple and Microsoft create separate ShopKeep accounts. If inventory looks
      empty, confirm the active provider before assuming data was lost. Signing in
      with the other provider opens that provider’s separate inventory.
    </p>
    <p>
      Support will not ask for passwords, verification codes, Apple authorization
      codes, Microsoft bearer tokens, deletion-retry tokens, or encrypted provider
      credentials.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="media" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Private photos and documents</h2>
    <p>
      ShopKeep stores media in the selected account’s SQLite database and returns
      it only through authenticated, account-scoped, no-store requests. A raw
      media request is not a public share link.
    </p>
    <p>
      If media stops loading, confirm the correct provider session, reconnect, and
      reopen the tool. A generic not-found response can mean the item belongs to a
      different account, was permanently removed, or is not available to the
      current bearer session; it does not reveal another account’s inventory.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="offline" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Installable PWA and offline limits</h2>
    <p>
      ShopKeep has no offline inventory mode. The native app has no local database
      mirror, write queue, or persistent media cache; it fetches inventory from the
      Azure service and keeps media only in memory. The web client can install an
      application shell, but inventory, authenticated media, exports, account
      changes, and deletion remain online operations. A visible shell is not a data
      backup.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="export" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Exports and recovery</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>CSV inventory</strong> is suitable for rows and spreadsheet review.</li>
      <li><strong>Location-label CSV</strong> carries location, sub-location, and QR data.</li>
      <li><strong>Insurance PDF dossier</strong> is a formatted report, not a restorable database.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Database backup</strong> is a downloadable SQLite copy and can
        include sensitive photos and documents stored as BLOBs.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      ShopKeep also keeps up to 14 local operator recovery bundles. An optional
      protected off-host exporter can publish private recovery copies to Azure
      Blob storage when enabled. Operator backups are not a substitute for keeping
      your own export.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="deletion" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Delete or recreate a ShopKeep account</h2>
    <p>
      In the private native build, open <strong>Settings → Account &amp;
      Data</strong>, review the deletion scope, and confirm
      <strong>Delete ShopKeep Account</strong>. The app clears local credentials,
      caches, widgets, search state, and temporary exports only after the server
      confirms the selected account was deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      If deletion fails, the account remains active and the app provides a recovery
      path; do not assume the data is gone. Contact support with the provider,
      build, time, and visible error. Physical-device verification is still a
      release gate, so report any mismatch rather than repeating destructive steps.
    </p>
    <p>
      Deletion affects only the active ShopKeep account. It does not delete the
      Apple or Microsoft account or the other provider’s ShopKeep account. A later
      fresh sign-in can create a new empty generation; it does not restore deleted
      inventory from an old session.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Troubleshooting checklist</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm web versus native and record the app or browser version.</li>
      <li>Confirm the Apple or Microsoft provider used for the affected inventory.</li>
      <li>Reconnect, reopen the tool, and retry one failed save or media load.</li>
      <li>Keep original documents and make an export before destructive recovery.</li>
      <li>
        For a repeated failure, record the time, tool identifier, action, and
        visible recovery message without sending credentials.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" class="legal-section">
    <h2>Contact and legal documents</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the
      platform, version, sign-in provider, affected feature, and steps already
      tried. Do not send tokens, passwords, payment details, or an unredacted
      database backup unless support requests a specific safe sample.
    </p>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/shopkeep/privacy">ShopKeep Privacy Policy</a> for storage,
      providers, exports, backups, and account-lifecycle boundaries. Use of
      ShopKeep is subject to the <a href="/terms">Nintek Terms of Use</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
